Split verify_composed into byte decoding and a verify over the parsed statement.

Part of the verifier-only build of SASH eb95bfa that the SP1 segment guest runs
(verifiable-inference-ethereum SPEC.md §1.1). Upstream source is Apache-2.0;
this patch modifies it (Apache-2.0 §4(b)).

The segment check parses `Fixed` itself, checks its own rules on it and on its
`Plan`, then verifies. Through the byte entry it would parse `Fixed` and run
`Plan::new` a second time.

- prover/src/compose.rs: verify_composed keeps its three decodes and their
  rejections, builds `Plan::new(&fixed.params)` as before, and returns
  `verify_composed_parsed(&fixed, &plan, &claims, proof)`. The new
  `pub fn verify_composed_parsed(fixed: &Fixed, plan: &Plan, claims: &Claims,
  proof: Proof) -> Verdict` is the rest of the old body, unchanged but for
  reading `fixed`, `plan` and `claims` through references; its caller passes
  the `Plan` of the same `fixed.params`. With `prover`, `t0` now starts in
  verify_composed_parsed, so `Verdict.verify_secs` no longer counts the JSON
  decoding; nothing else in the `Verdict` moves.

--- a/prover/src/compose.rs
+++ b/prover/src/compose.rs
